From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Micay <danielmicay@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jun 2017 03:23:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] x86: guarantee brk gap is at least one page

Per PaX, but for this alternate brk randomization approach.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Micay <danielmicay@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit efd85fdb08c06ecc1473c3a26a709ccf6591995d)
---
 arch/x86/kernel/process.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/process.c b/arch/x86/kernel/process.c
index 5a16bd90f96ee90065113f56f8fd6c4777e279fc..7d00430ec6c54260659adbe0fb54e3803cd4ded1 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/process.c
@@ -1028,9 +1028,9 @@ unsigned long arch_align_stack(unsigned long sp)
 unsigned long arch_randomize_brk(struct mm_struct *mm)
 {
 	if (mmap_is_ia32())
-		return mm->brk + get_random_long() % SZ_32M;
+		return mm->brk + get_random_long() % SZ_32M + PAGE_SIZE;
 
-	return mm->brk + get_random_long() % SZ_1G;
+	return mm->brk + get_random_long() % SZ_1G + PAGE_SIZE;
 }
 
